{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DDXpdM7ndJmPnaNqb5qZS7","type":"tool_result","content":"   298→\n   299→## 8. Simulation state model\n   300→\n   301→## 8.1 Core state container\n   302→\n   303→```rust\n   304→pub struct TankState {\n   305→    pub meta: SimMeta,\n   306→    pub geometry: TankGeometry,\n   307→    pub environment: EnvironmentState,\n   308→    pub hardware: HardwareState,\n   309→    pub water: WaterState,\n   310→    pub substrate: Vec<SubstrateLayerState>,\n   311→    pub filter: FilterState,\n   312→    pub plants: Vec<PlantGuildState>,\n   313→    pub algae: AlgaeState,\n   314→    pub microbes: MicrobeState,\n   315→    pub microfauna: MicrofaunaState,\n   316→    pub animals: AnimalState,\n   317→    pub detritus: DetritusState,\n   318→    pub schedules: ScheduleState,\n   319→    pub observables: ObservableState,\n   320→    pub events: Vec<SimEvent>,\n   321→    pub rng: SimRng,\n   322→}\n   323→```\n   324→\n   325→## 8.2 Environment state\n   326→\n   327→```rust\n   328→pub struct EnvironmentState {\n   329→    pub ambient_temp_c: f32,\n   330→    pub ambient_temp_schedule: AmbientSchedule,\n   331→    pub room_light_leak: f32, // 0..1, optional future use\n   332→    pub season_day: u16,\n   333→}\n   334→```\n   335→\n   336→### Ambient temperature action\n   337→Ambient temperature must be editable by the player at runtime. This represents room heating/cooling, seasonal weather, AC failure, or relocation of the tank.\n   338→\n   339→This action must affect:\n   340→- water temperature trends\n   341→- heater load\n   342→- dissolved oxygen saturation\n   343→- plant/algae rates\n   344→- shrimp stress and reproduction\n   345→- ammonia risk indirectly through temperature and pH-sensitive chemistry\n   346→\n   347→## 8.3 Hardware state\n   348→\n   349→```rust\n   350→pub struct HardwareState {\n   351→    pub light: LightState,\n   352→    pub heater: Option<HeaterState>,\n   353→    pub filter_pump: FilterPumpState,\n   354→    pub aeration: AerationState,\n   355→}\n   356→```\n   357→\n   358→### Light\n   359→```rust\n   360→pub struct LightState {\n   361→    pub enabled: bool,\n   362→    pub photoperiod_hours: f32,\n   363→    pub intensity_index: f32,      // relative scalar for v1\n   364→    pub par_surface_umol: f32,     // optional if known\n   365→    pub schedule_start_hour: u8,\n   366→}\n   367→```\n   368→\n   369→### Heater\n   370→```rust\n   371→pub struct HeaterState {\n   372→    pub enabled: bool,\n   373→    pub setpoint_c: f32,\n   374→    pub max_watts: f32,\n   375→    pub deadband_c: f32,\n   376→    pub efficiency: f32,\n   377→}\n   378→```\n   379→\n   380→### Filter / aeration\n   381→```rust\n   382→pub struct FilterPumpState {\n   383→    pub flow_lph: f32,\n   384→    pub media_surface_area_m2: f32,\n   385→    pub cleanliness: f32,  // 0..1\n   386→}\n   387→\n   388→pub struct AerationState {\n   389→    pub enabled: bool,\n   390→    pub intensity: f32,    // relative scalar\n   391→}\n   392→```\n   393→\n   394→## 8.4 Water state\n   395→\n   396→Internal water chemistry should primarily store **amounts** plus some derived state. Concentrations are derived from amount / volume.\n   397→\n   398→```rust\n   399→pub struct WaterState {\n   400→    pub volume_l: f32,\n   401→    pub temp_c: f32,\n   402→\n   403→    // Nitrogen\n   404→    pub ammonia_total_mg_n: f32,   // TAN = NH3 + NH4+, as N\n   405→    pub nitrite_mg_n: f32,\n   406→    pub nitrate_mg_n: f32,\n   407→\n   408→    // Phosphorus\n   409→    pub phosphate_mg_p: f32,\n   410→\n   411→    // Carbon / oxygen\n   412→    pub dissolved_oxygen_mg: f32,\n   413→    pub dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c: f32,\n   414→\n   415→    // Organic pools\n   416→    pub dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c: f32,\n   417→    pub dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n: f32,\n   418→\n   419→    // Major ions (minimum useful set)\n   420→    pub calcium_mg: f32,\n   421→    pub magnesium_mg: f32,\n   422→    pub sodium_mg: f32,\n   423→    pub potassium_mg: f32,\n   424→    pub bicarbonate_mg: f32,\n   425→    pub chloride_mg: f32,\n   426→    pub sulfate_mg: f32,\n   427→\n   428→    // Solver-facing water chemistry\n   429→    pub alkalinity_meq: f32,\n   430→    pub ph: f32,\n   431→    pub conductivity_us_cm: f32,\n   432→    pub tds_mg_l_display: f32,\n   433→}\n   434→```\n   435→\n   436→### Important rule\n   437→`TDS` must be a **derived display metric**, not the main hidden state. Internal modeling should use ions and alkalinity where possible.\n   438→\n   439→## 8.5 Substrate state\n   440→\n   441→Substrate must be layered.\n   442→\n   443→```rust\n   444→pub struct SubstrateLayerState {\n   445→    pub kind: SubstrateKind,\n   446→    pub depth_cm: f32,\n   447→    pub porosity: f32,\n   448→    pub cec_index: f32,               // cation exchange capacity proxy\n   449→    pub organic_matter_g: f32,\n   450→    pub trapped_detritus_g: f32,\n   451→    pub nutrient_store_n_mg: f32,\n   452→    pub nutrient_store_p_mg: f32,\n   453→    pub oxygen_penetration_index: f32,\n   454→    pub colonizable_area_m2: f32,\n   455→}\n   456→```\n   457→\n   458→### Required v1 substrate kinds\n   459→- inert sand\n   460→- inert gravel\n   461→- nutrient-rich planted substrate\n   462→- porous rubble / biomedia-like coarse layer\n   463→\n   464→Substrate must affect:\n   465→- rooted nutrient access\n   466→- detritus trapping\n   467→- microbial habitat\n   468→- potential low-oxygen zones\n   469→- shrimp grazing surface\n   470→\n   471→## 8.6 Filter state\n   472→\n   473→```rust\n   474→pub struct FilterState {\n   475→    pub maturity: f32,                // 0..1 summary metric\n   476→    pub ammonia_oxidizer_biomass: f32,\n   477→    pub nitrite_oxidizer_biomass: f32,\n   478→    pub comammox_biomass: f32,\n   479→    pub heterotroph_biomass: f32,\n   480→    pub clogging: f32,\n   481→}\n   482→```\n   483→\n   484→## 8.7 Plant guild state\n   485→\n   486→Plants are modeled as guilds, not per-leaf geometry.\n   487→\n   488→```rust\n   489→pub enum PlantGuildKind {\n   490→    FastStem,\n   491→    RootFeedingRosette,\n   492→    MossEpiphyte,\n   493→    FloatingPlant,\n   494→}\n   495→\n   496→pub struct PlantGuildState {\n   497→    pub kind: PlantGuildKind,\n   498→    pub name: String,\n   499→    pub biomass_g_dry: f32,\n   500→    pub health: f32,                  // 0..1\n   501→    pub nutrient_reserve_index: f32,  // 0..1\n   502→    pub shade_factor: f32,            // 0..1\n   503→    pub root_fraction: f32,\n   504→    pub growth_potential: f32,\n   505→}\n   506→```\n   507→\n   508→At minimum, v1 must include:\n   509→- one fast-growing water-column user\n   510→- one rooted/substrate-responsive plant guild\n   511→\n   512→## 8.8 Algae state\n   513→\n   514→```rust\n   515→pub struct AlgaeState {\n   516→    pub suspended_algae_biomass: f32,   // green water\n   517→    pub surface_film_biomass: f32,      // glass/film algae\n   518→    pub periphyton_biomass: f32,        // attached biofilm + algae complex\n   519→    pub nuisance_index: f32,            // 0..1 summary for UI\n   520→}\n   521→```\n   522→\n   523→## 8.9 Microbe state\n   524→\n   525→```rust\n   526→pub struct MicrobeState {\n   527→    pub decomposer_biomass: f32,\n   528→    pub ammonia_oxidizer_biomass: f32,\n   529→    pub nitrite_oxidizer_biomass: f32,\n   530→    pub comammox_biomass: f32,\n   531→    pub mineralization_capacity: f32,\n   532→}\n   533→```\n   534→\n   535→## 8.10 Microfauna state\n   536→\n   537→```rust\n   538→pub struct MicrofaunaState {\n   539→    pub bacterivorous_protists: f32,\n   540→    pub rotifers: f32,\n   541→    pub nematodes: f32,\n   542→    pub microcrustaceans: f32,\n   543→    pub visibility_index: f32,\n   544→}\n   545→```\n   546→\n   547→Microfauna are mostly hidden from the player in v1, but their effects are not optional.\n   548→\n   549→## 8.11 Animal state (v1 shrimp focus)\n   550→\n   551→```rust\n   552→pub struct AnimalState {\n   553→    pub shrimp: ShrimpPopulationState,\n   554→}\n   555→\n   556→pub struct ShrimpPopulationState {\n   557→    pub adults: u32,\n   558→    pub juveniles: u32,\n   559→    pub berried_females: u32,\n   560→    pub average_condition: f32,        // 0..1\n   561→    pub molt_stress_index: f32,        // 0..1\n   562→    pub reproductive_readiness: f32,   // 0..1\n   563→    pub egg_progress_days: f32,\n   564→}\n   565→```\n   566→\n   567→## 8.12 Detritus state\n   568→\n   569→```rust\n   570→pub struct DetritusState {\n   571→    pub particulate_organic_matter_g: f32,\n   572→    pub fine_detritus_g: f32,\n   573→    pub bioavailable_food_g: f32,\n   574→}\n   575→```\n   576→\n   577→---\n   578→\n   579→## 9. Observables vs hidden state\n   580→\n   581→The engine must distinguish:\n   582→\n   583→### Hidden internal state\n   584→Used for causality and simulation:\n   585→- microbial biomasses\n   586→- nutrient stores in substrate\n   587→- microfauna pools\n   588→- exact detrital pools\n   589→- internal maturity indices\n   590→\n   591→### Observable state\n   592→Shown to user:\n   593→- temperature\n   594→- pH\n   595→- GH / KH\n   596→- TDS\n   597→- conductivity\n   598→- DO\n   599→- TAN / nitrite / nitrate / phosphate\n   600→- plant health and growth direction\n   601→- algae risk\n   602→- shrimp population and condition\n   603→- biofilter maturity\n   604→- event log\n   605→- warnings/explanations\n   606→\n   607→This separation allows scientific depth without drowning the player in hidden variables.\n   608→\n   609→---\n   610→\n   611→## 10. Core simulation rules\n   612→\n   613→## 10.1 Temperature model\n   614→\n   615→Water temperature must be dynamic.\n   616→\n   617→Required equation family:\n   618→\n   619→```text\n   620→dT/dt = (Q_ambient + Q_heater + Q_light - Q_evap) / heat_capacity\n   621→```\n   622→\n   623→Where:\n   624→\n   625→- `heat_capacity` is proportional to tank water mass\n   626→- `Q_ambient` is based on temperature difference between ambient air and water and a geometry-dependent transfer coefficient\n   627→- `Q_heater` depends on heater power and thermostat logic\n   628→- `Q_light` is optional heating from lights\n   629→- `Q_evap` may be omitted in v1 and added later\n   630→\n   631→### Minimum v1 implementation\n   632→Use:\n   633→\n   634→```text\n   635→Q_ambient = UA_total * (T_ambient - T_water)\n   636→UA_total = k_surface * surface_area + k_walls * wall_area\n   637→heat_capacity = water_volume_l * 4186 J/K approximately\n   638→```\n   639→\n   640→### Acceptance behavior\n   641→- small open tanks respond faster to ambient changes than large tanks\n   642→- heaters partially buffer ambient swings\n   643→- if ambient exceeds heater setpoint, heater cannot cool the tank\n   644→- high ambient temperature reduces oxygen saturation and can stress shrimp\n   645→\n   646→## 10.2 Nitrogen cycle\n   647→\n   648→The minimum nitrogen pathway:\n   649→\n   650→```text\n   651→feed -> organic matter -> mineralization -> TAN -> nitrite -> nitrate\n   652→```\n   653→\n   654→### Inputs to TAN\n   655→- animal excretion\n   656→- decomposition/mineralization of detritus\n   657→- optional fertilizer dose\n   658→\n   659→### Outputs from TAN\n   660→- nitrification\n   661→- plant uptake\n   662→- water changes\n   663→\n   664→### Outputs from nitrite\n   665→- nitrite oxidation\n   666→- water changes\n   667→\n   668→### Outputs from nitrate\n   669→- plant uptake\n   670→- water changes\n   671→- optional denitrification in later phase\n   672→\n   673→### Required implementation rule\n   674→Nitrification must be biomass-limited, oxygen-limited, temperature-sensitive, and pH-sensitive.\n   675→\n   676→Do not implement nitrification as instant or as a fixed percentage independent of biology.\n   677→\n   678→Recommended generic rate form:\n   679→\n   680→```text\n   681→rate = Vmax * guild_biomass\n   682→     * f_temp(T)\n   683→     * f_pH(pH)\n   684→     * f_DO(DO)\n   685→     * substrate / (K + substrate)\n   686→```\n   687→\n   688→### Guild structure\n   689→v1 must support:\n   690→- ammonia oxidizers\n   691→- nitrite oxidizers\n   692→- comammox guild\n   693→\n   694→The agent may simplify by allowing comammox to oxidize TAN directly into nitrate with its own slower but efficient rate curve.\n   695→\n   696→## 10.3 Ammonia speciation and risk\n   697→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtcvhTKtbDxfRsSQuXRy5k","session_id":"aebe6b9c-6489-43f0-a717-82e4691947f3","uuid":"4e45027b-a05f-4c6d-b5de-6089d8cc75a8"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"acbccb342eb82c970","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtcvhTKtbDxfRsSQuXRy5k","description":"Reading spec.md","usage":{"total_tokens":33048,"tool_uses":16,"duration_ms":22168},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"dbb845cb-5005-4882-8d50-e8400bcd6aae","session_id":"aebe6b9c-6489-43f0-a717-82e4691947f3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_016bKMt6ZhqG6rYCdm7HdoJC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018zPqjkW2r2VjpB8PxMT4RP","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/root/tank-simulation/spec.md","offset":690,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4406,"cache_read_input_tokens":28580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4406,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtcvhTKtbDxfRsSQuXRy5k","session_id":"aebe6b9c-6489-43f0-a717-82e4691947f3","uuid":"12194502-b0b5-44a3-a067-80907965d98a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018zPqjkW2r2VjpB8PxMT4RP","type":"tool_result","content":"   690→- ammonia oxidizers\n   691→- nitrite oxidizers\n   692→- comammox guild\n   693→\n   694→The agent may simplify by allowing comammox to oxidize TAN directly into nitrate with its own slower but efficient rate curve.\n   695→\n   696→## 10.3 Ammonia speciation and risk\n   697→\n   698→Total ammonia is not enough. The engine must estimate the unionized fraction.\n   699→\n   700→Required approach:\n   701→- store total ammonia as TAN\n   702→- compute NH3 fraction from pH and temperature each tick\n   703→- use NH3-derived risk for toxicity/stress events\n   704→\n   705→Implementation note:\n   706→- use the freshwater equilibrium relation based on the Emerson et al. formulation commonly cited by EPA:\n   707→  - `pKa = 0.09018 + 2729.92 / (273.2 + T_celsius)`\n   708→  - `fraction_NH3 = 1 / (1 + 10^(pKa - pH))`\n   709→\n   710→Then:\n   711→```text\n   712→NH3_mg_n_per_l = TAN_mg_n_per_l * fraction_NH3\n   713→NH4_mg_n_per_l = TAN_mg_n_per_l - NH3_mg_n_per_l\n   714→```\n   715→\n   716→NH3 should drive acute risk more strongly than TAN.\n   717→\n   718→## 10.4 Oxygen and gas exchange\n   719→\n   720→The engine must track dissolved oxygen explicitly.\n   721→\n   722→### Sources\n   723→- plant photosynthesis (light-dependent)\n   724→- periphyton photosynthesis\n   725→- atmospheric reaeration\n   726→- aeration equipment\n   727→\n   728→### Sinks\n   729→- animal respiration\n   730→- plant respiration\n   731→- microbial respiration\n   732→- decomposition\n   733→- nitrification oxygen demand\n   734→\n   735→Recommended v1 form:\n   736→\n   737→```text\n   738→dDO/dt = photosynthesis\n   739→       + kLa_DO * (DO_sat(T) - DO)\n   740→       - respiration_total\n   741→       - nitrification_O2_cost\n   742→```\n   743→\n   744→### Required behaviors\n   745→- DO saturation decreases as temperature rises\n   746→- night-time oxygen can dip in planted tanks\n   747→- strong aeration increases gas exchange\n   748→- overfeeding increases oxygen demand via decomposition\n   749→\n   750→CO2/DIC may be modeled at lower fidelity in v1, but DO is mandatory.\n   751→\n   752→## 10.5 pH / alkalinity\n   753→\n   754→The engine must not treat pH as completely arbitrary.\n   755→\n   756→### Minimum acceptable v1\n   757→Track:\n   758→- alkalinity / KH\n   759→- dissolved inorganic carbon\n   760→- acidifying effect of nitrification\n   761→- degassing and photosynthesis effects on DIC\n   762→\n   763→Then solve or approximate pH each tick from alkalinity + DIC + temperature.\n   764→\n   765→### If full carbonate solver is too heavy for initial milestone\n   766→Temporary fallback:\n   767→- maintain pH as a derived approximation from KH and DIC\n   768→- document this as a temporary simplification\n   769→- do not hardcode pH as constant if plants, nitrification, and water changes occur\n   770→\n   771→## 10.6 Major ions, GH, KH, TDS\n   772→\n   773→v1 must track a minimal ion set sufficient to derive:\n   774→- GH from Ca + Mg\n   775→- KH / alkalinity from bicarbonate/alkalinity\n   776→- TDS display from dissolved ions\n   777→- conductivity display from ion content or empirical conversion\n   778→\n   779→This is required because the project explicitly cares about TDS and mineral conditions.\n   780→\n   781→### Required rule\n   782→Water changes and top-offs must mix source water chemistry into current tank water; they must not simply “reset numbers.”\n   783→\n   784→## 10.7 Plant growth\n   785→\n   786→Plants should not just be decorative biomass.\n   787→\n   788→Plant growth must depend on:\n   789→- available light\n   790→- water temperature\n   791→- nutrient availability\n   792→- access to nutrients from water and/or substrate depending on guild\n   793→- self-shading\n   794→- algae/periphyton competition\n   795→- stress from poor chemistry\n   796→\n   797→Recommended rate structure:\n   798→\n   799→```text\n   800→plant_growth = biomass\n   801→             * f_light\n   802→             * f_temp\n   803→             * min(f_nitrogen, f_phosphorus, f_carbon)\n   804→             * habitat_factor\n   805→             - respiration\n   806→             - senescence\n   807→```\n   808→\n   809→### Guild differences\n   810→- fast stem plants: stronger water-column nutrient uptake, faster growth, stronger shading feedback\n   811→- root-feeding plants: benefit more from nutrient-rich sediment and adequate substrate depth\n   812→- moss/epiphytes: more surface-attached, low root dependence\n   813→- floating plants: strong light access, strong nutrient uptake, high shading effect\n   814→\n   815→### Required behavior\n   816→Nutrient-rich substrate must benefit rooted plants more than inert substrate.\n   817→\n   818→## 10.8 Algae and periphyton\n   819→\n   820→Separate at least:\n   821→- suspended algae\n   822→- attached film/periphyton\n   823→\n   824→Growth drivers:\n   825→- light\n   826→- excess nutrients\n   827→- temperature\n   828→- low grazing pressure\n   829→- weak plant competition\n   830→- surface availability (for attached forms)\n   831→\n   832→Recommended structure:\n   833→\n   834→```text\n   835→algae_growth = biomass\n   836→             * f_light\n   837→             * f_temp\n   838→             * min(f_nitrogen, f_phosphorus)\n   839→             * competition_modifier\n   840→             - grazing\n   841→             - sloughing\n   842→```\n   843→\n   844→### Required behavior\n   845→The system must support:\n   846→- green-water style blooms when nutrients/light are favorable\n   847→- film/periphyton increase on surfaces under imbalance\n   848→- attached biofilm as both nuisance and shrimp food source\n   849→\n   850→## 10.9 Biofilm / periphyton role\n   851→\n   852→Periphyton is not merely “algae.” It is a mixed guild that includes autotrophs and heterotrophs and should be treated as an ecological intermediary.\n   853→\n   854→Periphyton must:\n   855→- provide shrimp grazing resource\n   856→- contribute to oxygen and nutrient dynamics\n   857→- increase with available surface area and light/nutrients\n   858→- support microfauna habitat\n   859→- become nuisance at high biomass\n   860→\n   861→## 10.10 Decomposition and mineralization\n   862→\n   863→Detritus must move through at least these pools:\n   864→\n   865→```text\n   866→particulate food/waste -> fine detritus -> dissolved organics -> mineralized nutrients\n   867→```\n   868→\n   869→Rates depend on:\n   870→- temperature\n   871→- decomposer biomass\n   872→- oxygen\n   873→- detritus quality\n   874→- substrate trapping\n   875→\n   876→Overfeeding must increase:\n   877→- detritus\n   878→- microbial oxygen demand\n   879→- TAN generation\n   880→- algae risk\n   881→\n   882→## 10.11 Microfauna\n   883→\n   884→Microfauna should be abstracted as guilds with real effects.\n   885→\n   886→Minimum effects:\n   887→- bacterivorous protists reduce bacterial standing biomass but enhance nutrient turnover\n   888→- rotifers/nematodes/microcrustaceans compete for biofilm resources\n   889→- shrimp grazing/predation suppresses some microfauna pools\n   890→\n   891→Player does not need exact counts, but the engine must use these pools in ecology.\n   892→\n   893→## 10.12 Shrimp physiology and population\n   894→\n   895→`Neocaridina davidi` is the target reference species for v1.\n   896→\n   897→The shrimp model must include:\n   898→- adults\n   899→- juveniles\n   900→- berried females\n   901→- condition\n   902→- molt stress\n   903→- reproduction readiness\n   904→- juvenile survival\n   905→\n   906→### Inputs affecting shrimp condition\n   907→- food availability\n   908→- biofilm availability\n   909→- temperature\n   910→- DO\n   911→- NH3 risk\n   912→- nitrite risk\n   913→- mineral status (GH / ion adequacy proxy)\n   914→- instability / sudden swings\n   915→\n   916→### Reproduction\n   917→A simple but meaningful model:\n   918→\n   919→```text\n   920→spawn_probability =\n   921→    f_temperature\n   922→  * f_condition\n   923→  * f_stability\n   924→  * f_mineral_status\n   925→  * sex_ratio_proxy\n   926→```\n   927→\n   928→When spawning succeeds:\n   929→- berried female count increases\n   930→- egg development progresses over days\n   931→- hatch success depends on stress during egg period\n   932→\n   933→### Molting\n   934→Molting stress rises when:\n   935→- mineral conditions are poor\n   936→- temperature is stressful\n   937→- rapid chemistry swings occur\n   938→- condition is poor\n   939→\n   940→### Mortality\n   941→Mortality should be probabilistic, with risk increased by:\n   942→- NH3\n   943→- severe nitrite\n   944→- low oxygen\n   945→- prolonged thermal stress\n   946→- failed molt stress\n   947→- starvation / collapse of biofilm and food web\n   948→\n   949→---\n   950→\n   951→## 11. Player actions\n   952→\n   953→Actions are part of the simulation API.\n   954→\n   955→## 11.1 Setup actions\n   956→\n   957→- choose tank dimensions and fill height\n   958→- choose substrate type(s) and depth\n   959→- choose filter and media\n   960→- choose heater and setpoint\n   961→- choose light intensity and photoperiod\n   962→- define source water chemistry\n   963→- add plants\n   964→- add shrimp\n   965→- optionally seed filter/media\n   966→\n   967→## 11.2 Runtime husbandry actions\n   968→\n   969→The engine MUST support at least:\n   970→\n   971→```rust\n   972→pub enum PlayerAction {\n   973→    Feed { grams: f32 },\n   974→    WaterChangePercent { percent: f32, source: SourceWaterProfile },\n   975→    TopOffEvaporation { liters: f32, source: SourceWaterProfile },\n   976→    DoseFertilizer { n_mg: f32, p_mg: f32, k_mg: f32 },\n   977→    TrimPlants { fraction: f32 },\n   978→    SiphonDetritus { fraction: f32 },\n   979→    CleanFilter { intensity: f32 },\n   980→    AddShrimp { count: u32 },\n   981→    RemoveShrimp { count: u32 },\n   982→    ChangePhotoperiod { hours: f32 },\n   983→    ChangeLightIntensity { intensity_index: f32 },\n   984→    ChangeHeaterSetpoint { setpoint_c: f32 },\n   985→    ChangeAmbientTemperature { target_c: f32 },\n   986→    ChangeAeration { enabled: bool, intensity: f32 },\n   987→}\n   988→```\n   989→\n   990→### Important requirement\n   991→`ChangeAmbientTemperature` is mandatory in the public API.\n   992→\n   993→## 11.3 Action semantics\n   994→\n   995→### Feed\n   996→- adds particulate organics\n   997→- increases later detritus and excretion\n   998→- increases food availability\n   999→- may improve reproduction if not excessive\n  1000→\n  1001→### Water change\n  1002→- removes dissolved and suspended constituents proportionally\n  1003→- mixes in source water temperature and chemistry\n  1004→- can cause stress if parameters differ strongly\n  1005→\n  1006→### Top-off\n  1007→- restores volume but usually does not remove dissolved waste\n  1008→- depending on source chemistry, can alter TDS/KH/GH\n  1009→\n  1010→### Clean filter\n  1011→- reduces clogging\n  1012→- may remove nitrifier biomass if too aggressive\n  1013→\n  1014→### Change ambient temperature\n  1015→- changes room environment, not instant water temperature\n  1016→- effect propagates through heat transfer over time\n  1017→\n  1018→---\n  1019→\n  1020→## 12. Update order per tick\n  1021→\n  1022→The order must be explicit and stable.\n  1023→\n  1024→Recommended hourly update pipeline:\n  1025→\n  1026→1. apply scheduled environment updates\n  1027→2. apply queued player actions\n  1028→3. update water volume (evaporation/top-off/water change)\n  1029→4. update temperature from ambient + heater + equipment\n  1030→5. update light state for current hour\n  1031→6. compute gas solubility targets from temperature\n  1032→7. process feeding/excretion pulses\n  1033→8. move detritus through decomposition/mineralization\n  1034→9. update nitrification\n  1035→10. update carbon/oxygen exchange\n  1036→11. update plant photosynthesis/respiration\n  1037→12. update algae/periphyton photosynthesis/respiration\n  1038→13. update pH / alkalinity / NH3 fraction\n  1039→14. update shrimp feeding/stress\n  1040→15. accumulate daily summaries\n  1041→16. emit events / warnings / observations\n  1042→17. recompute observables\n  1043→\n  1044→Daily update pipeline:\n  1045→\n  1046→1. plant biomass growth/senescence\n  1047→2. algae net biomass changes\n  1048→3. microfauna turnover\n  1049→4. shrimp reproduction and juvenile recruitment\n  1050→5. mortality checks\n  1051→6. biofilter maturity trend updates\n  1052→7. weekly/monthly counters if needed\n  1053→\n  1054→---\n  1055→\n  1056→## 13. Event and explanation system\n  1057→\n  1058→The simulation must produce interpretable events.\n  1059→\n  1060→```rust\n  1061→pub struct SimEvent {\n  1062→    pub day: u32,\n  1063→    pub severity: EventSeverity,\n  1064→    pub kind: EventKind,\n  1065→    pub summary: String,\n  1066→    pub causes: Vec<String>,\n  1067→}\n  1068→```\n  1069→\n  1070→Required event kinds:\n  1071→- cycle progressing\n  1072→- ammonia warning\n  1073→- nitrite warning\n  1074→- oxygen dip\n  1075→- algae bloom risk rising\n  1076→- algae bloom underway\n  1077→- biofilm maturity increase\n  1078→- shrimp berried\n  1079→- egg drop / reproductive failure\n  1080→- molt stress warning\n  1081→- filter cleaning setback\n  1082→- substrate fouling warning\n  1083→- stability improving\n  1084→\n  1085→Example:\n  1086→```text\n  1087→Day 41: Moderate warning — night oxygen dip\n  1088→Causes:\n  1089→- high detritus after heavy feeding"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtcvhTKtbDxfRsSQuXRy5k","session_id":"aebe6b9c-6489-43f0-a717-82e4691947f3","uuid":"1502d2e4-fcf9-475e-9626-69c75123224c"}
