{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YQVJ9ioXApazUuxNgUCyZf","type":"tool_result","content":"  1080→- molt stress warning\n  1081→- filter cleaning setback\n  1082→- substrate fouling warning\n  1083→- stability improving\n  1084→\n  1085→Example:\n  1086→```text\n  1087→Day 41: Moderate warning — night oxygen dip\n  1088→Causes:\n  1089→- high detritus after heavy feeding\n  1090→- strong plant biomass increased night respiration\n  1091→- low aeration\n  1092→- warm ambient temperature reduced oxygen saturation\n  1093→```\n  1094→\n  1095→This layer is essential for learning and gameplay.\n  1096→\n  1097→---\n  1098→\n  1099→## 14. Persistence and data-driven content\n  1100→\n  1101→## 14.1 Config files\n  1102→\n  1103→Use serialized config files for:\n  1104→- tank presets\n  1105→- source water profiles\n  1106→- substrate types\n  1107→- plant guild packs\n  1108→- shrimp species packs\n  1109→- process parameter sets\n  1110→- scenarios\n  1111→\n  1112→## 14.2 Parameter provenance\n  1113→\n  1114→Every important parameter should support metadata:\n  1115→\n  1116→```rust\n  1117→pub struct Parameter<T> {\n  1118→    pub value: T,\n  1119→    pub unit: String,\n  1120→    pub source_title: String,\n  1121→    pub source_year: u16,\n  1122→    pub confidence: f32,      // 0..1\n  1123→    pub notes: String,\n  1124→}\n  1125→```\n  1126→\n  1127→This is required for scientific credibility and later calibration.\n  1128→\n  1129→## 14.3 Save files\n  1130→\n  1131→A save file must include:\n  1132→- full `TankState`\n  1133→- simulation version\n  1134→- RNG state\n  1135→- schema version\n  1136→\n  1137→A save should be resumable with bitwise-identical deterministic results if code version is unchanged.\n  1138→\n  1139→---\n  1140→\n  1141→## 15. Rust workspace structure\n  1142→\n  1143→Recommended workspace:\n  1144→\n  1145→```text\n  1146→aquarium-sim/\n  1147→  Cargo.toml\n  1148→  crates/\n  1149→    tank_core/\n  1150→    tank_data/\n  1151→    tank_tui/\n  1152→    tank_scenarios/\n  1153→    tank_cli/        # optional launcher\n  1154→```\n  1155→\n  1156→## 15.1 `tank_core`\n  1157→\n  1158→Contains:\n  1159→- state types\n  1160→- update systems\n  1161→- equations\n  1162→- action application\n  1163→- save/load schema\n  1164→- tests\n  1165→- deterministic RNG wrapper\n  1166→\n  1167→No UI dependencies allowed.\n  1168→\n  1169→## 15.2 `tank_data`\n  1170→\n  1171→Contains:\n  1172→- TOML/JSON/RON assets\n  1173→- parameter loading\n  1174→- validation of configs\n  1175→- preset species and scenario packs\n  1176→\n  1177→## 15.3 `tank_tui`\n  1178→\n  1179→Contains:\n  1180→- terminal dashboard\n  1181→- input mapping\n  1182→- time controls\n  1183→- screens/tabs\n  1184→- charts / sparkline widgets\n  1185→\n  1186→## 15.4 `tank_scenarios`\n  1187→\n  1188→Contains:\n  1189→- sample scenarios\n  1190→- regression validation scenarios\n  1191→- benchmark presets (nano tank, medium planted tank, warm-room stress case, etc.)\n  1192→\n  1193→---\n  1194→\n  1195→## 16. Suggested crate/tool choices\n  1196→\n  1197→These are recommendations, not hard requirements.\n  1198→\n  1199→- `serde` for serialization/deserialization\n  1200→- `thiserror` for typed errors\n  1201→- `rand_chacha` or another deterministic RNG\n  1202→- `ratatui` for terminal UI\n  1203→- `tracing` for instrumentation\n  1204→- `uom` or a lightweight custom units layer if desired\n  1205→- `approx` for float comparisons in tests\n  1206→\n  1207→Do **not** couple the core to a graphics engine in v1.\n  1208→\n  1209→---\n  1210→\n  1211→## 17. Public engine API\n  1212→\n  1213→```rust\n  1214→pub trait SimulationEngine {\n  1215→    fn apply_action(&mut self, action: PlayerAction) -> Result<(), SimError>;\n  1216→    fn step_hours(&mut self, hours: u32) -> Result<(), SimError>;\n  1217→    fn snapshot(&self) -> TankSnapshot;\n  1218→    fn full_state(&self) -> &TankState;\n  1219→}\n  1220→```\n  1221→\n  1222→### Snapshot\n  1223→`TankSnapshot` should expose UI-friendly derived values without requiring the UI to know the low-level chemistry model.\n  1224→\n  1225→```rust\n  1226→pub struct TankSnapshot {\n  1227→    pub day: u32,\n  1228→    pub temp_c: f32,\n  1229→    pub ph: f32,\n  1230→    pub do_mg_l: f32,\n  1231→    pub tan_mg_l: f32,\n  1232→    pub nh3_mg_l: f32,\n  1233→    pub nitrite_mg_l: f32,\n  1234→    pub nitrate_mg_l: f32,\n  1235→    pub phosphate_mg_l: f32,\n  1236→    pub gh_d: f32,\n  1237→    pub kh_d: f32,\n  1238→    pub conductivity_us_cm: f32,\n  1239→    pub tds_mg_l: f32,\n  1240→    pub plant_status: Vec<PlantStatusView>,\n  1241→    pub shrimp_status: ShrimpStatusView,\n  1242→    pub algae_risk: f32,\n  1243→    pub biofilter_maturity: f32,\n  1244→    pub recent_events: Vec<SimEvent>,\n  1245→}\n  1246→```\n  1247→\n  1248→---\n  1249→\n  1250→## 18. Numerical and modeling requirements\n  1251→\n  1252→## 18.1 Internal representation rules\n  1253→\n  1254→Prefer:\n  1255→- masses in mg or g\n  1256→- volumes in liters\n  1257→- temperatures in °C\n  1258→- times in hours/days\n  1259→- derived concentrations in mg/L\n  1260→- conductivity in µS/cm\n  1261→- GH/KH in degree equivalents only for display\n  1262→\n  1263→## 18.2 Clamping and invariants\n  1264→\n  1265→All update systems must enforce:\n  1266→- no negative masses\n  1267→- no negative populations\n  1268→- no temperature below freezing in normal freshwater scenarios unless explicitly allowed\n  1269→- `0.0 <= health <= 1.0`\n  1270→- `0.0 <= maturity <= 1.0`\n  1271→\n  1272→## 18.3 Stability\n  1273→\n  1274→Systems must avoid:\n  1275→- uncontrolled exponential blow-ups from naive multiplicative rates\n  1276→- order dependence caused by mutable global state without explicit pipeline\n  1277→- floating-point drift causing negative pools\n  1278→\n  1279→Where necessary:\n  1280→- clamp rates to available mass\n  1281→- use saturating subtraction\n  1282→- use bounded logistic or Monod-like functions\n  1283→\n  1284→---\n  1285→\n  1286→## 19. TUI requirements\n  1287→\n  1288→The terminal UI is part of the MVP.\n  1289→\n  1290→## 19.1 Minimum screens\n  1291→\n  1292→1. **Overview**\n  1293→   - day/time\n  1294→   - chemistry summary\n  1295→   - plant summary\n  1296→   - shrimp summary\n  1297→   - event warnings\n  1298→\n  1299→2. **Chemistry**\n  1300→   - temperature\n  1301→   - pH\n  1302→   - DO\n  1303→   - TAN / NH3 / nitrite / nitrate / phosphate\n  1304→   - GH/KH/TDS/conductivity\n  1305→   - trends over recent days\n  1306→\n  1307→3. **Biology**\n  1308→   - plants\n  1309→   - algae/periphyton\n  1310→   - shrimp population\n  1311→   - reproduction\n  1312→   - hidden-state summaries like biofilter maturity and microfauna health\n  1313→\n  1314→4. **Actions**\n  1315→   - feed\n  1316→   - water change\n  1317→   - trim\n  1318→   - siphon\n  1319→   - change ambient temp\n  1320→   - change light / heater settings\n  1321→\n  1322→5. **Event log**\n  1323→   - chronological causal log\n  1324→\n  1325→## 19.2 Time controls\n  1326→\n  1327→- advance 1 hour\n  1328→- advance 1 day\n  1329→- advance 1 week\n  1330→- pause/autoadvance\n  1331→\n  1332→---\n  1333→\n  1334→## 20. Acceptance tests and regression scenarios\n  1335→\n  1336→These are mandatory.\n  1337→\n  1338→## 20.1 Determinism test\n  1339→Given identical seed and action sequence, snapshots must match exactly or within fixed float tolerance.\n  1340→\n  1341→## 20.2 Mass balance test\n  1342→Water change removes the expected fraction of dissolved constituents.\n  1343→\n  1344→## 20.3 Tank-size stability test\n  1345→With identical feed mass and livestock addition:\n  1346→- 10 L tank must show larger concentration swings than 100 L tank\n  1347→- 10 L tank must change temperature faster after ambient temp jump\n  1348→\n  1349→## 20.4 Ambient temperature test\n  1350→Scenario:\n  1351→- stable tank at 24 °C\n  1352→- ambient raised to 31 °C\n  1353→Expected:\n  1354→- water warms over time, not instantly\n  1355→- DO saturation target falls\n  1356→- shrimp stress rises if sustained\n  1357→- heater usage drops to zero if heater present\n  1358→\n  1359→## 20.5 Cycling test\n  1360→Brand-new tanks with identical setup but different seeded states should show different time-to-stability.\n  1361→\n  1362→Expected:\n  1363→- TAN and nitrite do not disappear instantly\n  1364→- nitrifier biomass grows over time\n  1365→- filter cleaning early in the cycle can delay maturation\n  1366→\n  1367→## 20.6 Overfeeding test\n  1368→Repeated overfeeding must produce:\n  1369→- rising detritus\n  1370→- increased oxygen demand\n  1371→- TAN increase\n  1372→- elevated algae risk\n  1373→\n  1374→## 20.7 Rooted substrate test\n  1375→A rooted plant guild in nutrient-rich substrate must outperform the same guild in inert sand under otherwise equal conditions.\n  1376→\n  1377→## 20.8 Reproduction thermal stress test\n  1378→At high sustained temperature, shrimp reproduction readiness and success must fall relative to moderate temperature conditions.\n  1379→\n  1380→## 20.9 Water change chemistry shock test\n  1381→A large water change with very different GH/KH/TDS must improve some waste metrics while potentially increasing stress.\n  1382→\n  1383→---\n  1384→\n  1385→## 21. Milestone plan for an implementation agent\n  1386→\n  1387→## Milestone 0 — repository skeleton\n  1388→Deliver:\n  1389→- cargo workspace\n  1390→- core types\n  1391→- build/test CI\n  1392→- sample config loading\n  1393→- save/load roundtrip test\n  1394→\n  1395→## Milestone 1 — tank geometry and temperature\n  1396→Deliver:\n  1397→- `TankGeometry`\n  1398→- `EnvironmentState`\n  1399→- `HardwareState`\n  1400→- temperature update system\n  1401→- ambient temperature action\n  1402→- heater logic\n  1403→- tank-size comparison tests\n  1404→\n  1405→## Milestone 2 — dissolved pools and water changes\n  1406→Deliver:\n  1407→- `WaterState`\n  1408→- source water profiles\n  1409→- water change/top-off actions\n  1410→- TDS / GH / KH / conductivity derivation\n  1411→- chemistry snapshot rendering\n  1412→\n  1413→## Milestone 3 — nitrogen + oxygen cycle\n  1414→Deliver:\n  1415→- detritus pools\n  1416→- decomposition\n  1417→- nitrification guilds\n  1418→- oxygen dynamics\n  1419→- NH3 fraction calculation\n  1420→- event warnings\n  1421→\n  1422→## Milestone 4 — substrate + plants + algae\n  1423→Deliver:\n  1424→- substrate layers\n  1425→- plant guilds\n  1426→- algae/periphyton\n  1427→- light schedule\n  1428→- rooted vs water-column nutrient access\n  1429→- trim action\n  1430→\n  1431→## Milestone 5 — shrimp + microfauna\n  1432→Deliver:\n  1433→- shrimp population model\n  1434→- food-web linkage to biofilm/periphyton\n  1435→- reproduction / molt stress\n  1436→- high-temperature reproduction penalty\n  1437→- microfauna abstraction\n  1438→\n  1439→## Milestone 6 — TUI MVP\n  1440→Deliver:\n  1441→- overview/chemistry/biology/actions/log screens\n  1442→- time controls\n  1443→- scenario selection\n  1444→- save/load support\n  1445→\n  1446→## Milestone 7 — validation + balancing\n  1447→Deliver:\n  1448→- regression scenarios\n  1449→- parameter audit with provenance\n  1450→- balancing pass for plausible trajectories\n  1451→- documentation of known simplifications\n  1452→\n  1453→---\n  1454→\n  1455→## 22. Initial parameter packs required\n  1456→\n  1457→The first data pack must include:\n  1458→\n  1459→### Source water profile presets\n  1460→- soft acidic\n  1461→- moderate community-tank water\n  1462→- hard alkaline shrimp water\n  1463→- RO-like low-mineral water\n  1464→\n  1465→### Substrate presets\n  1466→- inert sand\n  1467→- inert gravel\n  1468→- active planted substrate\n  1469→- coarse porous media mix\n  1470→\n  1471→### Plant guild presets\n  1472→- fast stem\n  1473→- rooted rosette\n  1474→- moss/epiphyte\n  1475→- floating plant (optional v1.1)\n  1476→\n  1477→### Shrimp pack\n  1478→- `Neocaridina davidi`\n  1479→  - moderate temperature optimum"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtcvhTKtbDxfRsSQuXRy5k","session_id":"aebe6b9c-6489-43f0-a717-82e4691947f3","uuid":"93bdf276-34a6-4080-b686-d4fc87f05a81"}
