{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtcvhTKtbDxfRsSQuXRy5k","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have a complete picture. Let me provide the comprehensive report:\n\n## Complete Workspace Exploration Report\n\n### Project Status\n\nThis is a **pre-implementation stage** of a Rust workspace project. No Cargo.toml files or source code (.rs files) exist yet. The project consists entirely of specification and planning documents.\n\n**Git Status:**\n- Current branch: `ralph/tank-sim`\n- Latest commits:\n  - `184e6c2` - chore(tank-sim): sync initial prompt inputs\n  - `5fc621c` - Initial commit with project spec\n\n**Tracked Files in Repository:**\n- `/root/tank-simulation/spec.md` (1,588 lines) - Comprehensive implementation specification\n- `/root/tank-simulation/.ralph/projects/tank-sim/project.toml` - Project metadata\n- `/root/tank-simulation/.ralph/projects/tank-sim/prompt.md` - Implementation prompt (v1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Cargo Workspace Structure (Planned but not yet created)\n\nThe spec defines a workspace to be created at `/root/tank-simulation/` with 4 crates under `crates/`:\n\n1. **tank_core** - Main simulation engine\n   - State types and models\n   - Update systems and equations\n   - Action application logic\n   - Save/load schema\n   - Deterministic RNG wrapper\n   - Unit tests\n   - No UI dependencies\n\n2. **tank_data** - Configuration and data loading\n   - TOML/JSON/RON preset assets\n   - Parameter loading and validation\n   - Preset packs for species and scenarios\n\n3. **tank_tui** - Terminal user interface\n   - Terminal dashboard (ratatui-based)\n   - Input mapping\n   - Time controls\n   - 5 main screens (Overview, Chemistry, Biology, Actions, Log)\n   - Charts/sparklines\n\n4. **tank_scenarios** - Test fixtures and scenarios\n   - Sample scenarios\n   - Regression validation scenarios\n   - Benchmark presets (nano, medium, warm-room)\n\n---\n\n### 2. Core Data Types (Defined in spec but not yet implemented)\n\n#### Main State Container\n```\nTankState\n├── meta: SimMeta\n├── geometry: TankGeometry\n├── environment: EnvironmentState\n├── hardware: HardwareState\n├── water: WaterState\n├── substrate: Vec<SubstrateLayerState>\n├── filter: FilterState\n├── plants: Vec<PlantGuildState>\n├── algae: AlgaeState\n├── microbes: MicrobeState\n├── microfauna: MicrofaunaState\n├── animals: AnimalState\n├── detritus: DetritusState\n├── schedules: ScheduleState\n├── observables: ObservableState\n├── events: Vec<SimEvent>\n└── rng: SimRng\n```\n\n#### Geometry (TankGeometry)\n- `length_cm, width_cm, height_cm, fill_height_cm`\n- `glass_thickness_mm, open_top: bool`\n- Derives: water_volume_l, surface_area_cm2, wall_area_cm2, footprint_area_cm2, surface/wall area ratios\n\n#### Water Chemistry (WaterState)\n- **Nitrogen pools:** ammonia_total_mg_n, nitrite_mg_n, nitrate_mg_n\n- **Phosphorus:** phosphate_mg_p\n- **Carbon/Oxygen:** dissolved_oxygen_mg, dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c\n- **Organic pools:** dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c, dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n\n- **Major ions:** calcium_mg, magnesium_mg, sodium_mg, potassium_mg, bicarbonate_mg, chloride_mg, sulfate_mg\n- **Derived:** alkalinity_meq, ph, conductivity_us_cm, tds_mg_l_display\n\n#### Hardware\n- **Light:** enabled, photoperiod_hours, intensity_index, schedule_start_hour\n- **Heater:** enabled, setpoint_c, max_watts, deadband_c, efficiency\n- **Filter/Pump:** flow_lph, media_surface_area_m2, cleanliness (0..1)\n- **Aeration:** enabled, intensity\n\n#### Substrate (LayerState - 1-3 layers)\n- kind: SubstrateKind (inert sand, inert gravel, active planted, coarse porous)\n- depth_cm, porosity, cec_index, organic_matter_g, trapped_detritus_g\n- nutrient stores (N, P), oxygen_penetration_index, colonizable_area_m2\n\n#### Filter State\n- maturity: f32 (0..1)\n- ammonia_oxidizer_biomass, nitrite_oxidizer_biomass, comammox_biomass\n- heterotroph_biomass, clogging\n\n#### Plants (Guild-based, not individual)\n- PlantGuildKind: FastStem, RootFeedingRosette, MossEpiphyte, FloatingPlant\n- For each guild: name, biomass_g_dry, health (0..1), nutrient_reserve_index (0..1)\n- shade_factor (0..1), root_fraction, growth_potential\n\n#### Algae State\n- suspended_algae_biomass (green water)\n- surface_film_biomass (glass algae)\n- periphyton_biomass (attached biofilm complex)\n- nuisance_index (0..1)\n\n#### Microbes (Hidden state)\n- decomposer_biomass\n- ammonia_oxidizer_biomass, nitrite_oxidizer_biomass, comammox_biomass\n- mineralization_capacity\n\n#### Microfauna (Aggregated)\n- bacterivorous_protists, rotifers, nematodes, microcrustaceans\n- visibility_index (0..1)\n\n#### Shrimp Population (AnimalState)\n- adults, juveniles, berried_females (counts as u32)\n- average_condition (0..1)\n- molt_stress_index (0..1)\n- reproductive_readiness (0..1)\n- egg_progress_days\n\n#### Detritus State\n- particulate_organic_matter_g\n- fine_detritus_g\n- bioavailable_food_g\n\n#### Events\n- day: u32, hour: u8, severity, kind, causes: Vec<String>, summary\n- Required event kinds: CycleProgressing, AmmoniaWarning, NitriteWarning, OxygenDip, AlgaeRiskRising, AlgaeBloom, BiofilmMaturityIncrease, ShrimpBerried, EggFailure, MoltStressWarning, FilterCleaningSetback, SubstrateFoulingWarning, StabilityImproving\n- Keep last 200 events in state, expose last 20 to UI\n\n---\n\n### 3. Public API Traits and Enums (Defined in spec)\n\n#### SimulationEngine Trait\n```rust\npub trait SimulationEngine {\n    fn apply_action(&mut self, action: PlayerAction) -> Result<(), SimError>;\n    fn step_hours(&mut self, hours: u32) -> Result<(), SimError>;\n    fn snapshot(&self) -> TankSnapshot;\n    fn full_state(&self) -> &TankState;\n}\n```\n\n#### PlayerAction Enum\n- `Feed { grams: f64 }`\n- `WaterChangePercent { percent: f64, source_profile_id: String }`\n- `TrimPlants { fraction: f64 }`\n- `SiphonDetritus { fraction: f64 }`\n- `CleanFilter { intensity: f64 }`\n- `AddShrimp { count: u32 }`\n- `RemoveShrimp { count: u32 }`\n- `ChangePhotoperiod { hours: f64 }`\n- `ChangeLightIntensity { intensity_index: f64 }`\n- `ChangeHeaterSetpoint { setpoint_c: f64 }`\n- `ChangeAmbientTemperature { target_c: f64 }` (MANDATORY)\n- `ChangeAeration { enabled: bool, intensity: f64 }`\n\n#### TankSnapshot (UI-Friendly View)\n- day: u32, temp_c, ph, do_mg_l, tan_mg_l, nh3_mg_l\n- nitrite_mg_l, nitrate_mg_l, phosphate_mg_l\n- gh_d, kh_d, conductivity_us_cm, tds_mg_l\n- plant_status: Vec<PlantStatusView>\n- shrimp_status: ShrimpStatusView\n- algae_risk: f32, biofilter_maturity: f32\n- recent_events: Vec<SimEvent> (last 20)\n\n#### SimSeed(u64) - Deterministic RNG seeding\n\n---\n\n### 4. Key Modeling Systems\n\n#### Temperature Model\n- Heat capacity proportional to water mass: `heat_capacity_j_per_k = volume_l * 4186.0`\n- Heat transfer: `ua_total_w_per_k = (k_surface * surface_area_m2 * top_factor) + (k_wall * wall_area_m2)`\n- Ambient heat: `q_ambient_w = ua_total_w_per_k * (ambient_temp_c - water_temp_c)`\n- Heater (when enabled and below setpoint): `q_heater_w = max_watts * efficiency`\n- Heater must never cool the tank\n- Delta: `delta_temp_c = (q_ambient_w + q_heater_w) * dt_s / heat_capacity_j_per_k`\n\n#### Nitrogen Cycle\n- Pathway: feed → detritus → mineralization → TAN → nitrite → nitrate\n- Nitrification must be biomass-limited, oxygen-limited, temperature/pH-sensitive\n- Monod-style rate: `rate = vmax * biomass * f_temp * f_pH * f_do * substrate / (k_substrate + substrate)`\n- Nitrifier guilds: ammonia oxidizers (AOA), nitrite oxidizers (NOB), comammox\n- O2 demand: 4.57 mg O2 per 1 mg N nitrified to nitrate\n- Alkalinity consumed: 0.1428 meq per 1 mg N nitrified\n\n#### Ammonia Speciation\n- pKa = 0.09018 + 2729.92 / (273.2 + temp_c)\n- fraction_nh3 = 1.0 / (1.0 + 10^(pKa - ph))\n- nh3_mg_l = tan_mg_l * fraction_nh3\n- NH3 drives toxicity more strongly than TAN\n\n#### Dissolved Oxygen\n- DO saturation table (linear interpolation):\n  - 0°C → 14.6 mg/L\n  - 10°C → 11.3 mg/L\n  - 20°C → 9.1 mg/L\n  - 30°C → 7.6 mg/L\n- Sources: photosynthesis (plants, periphyton), reaeration (kLa-based), aeration equipment\n- Sinks: respiration (shrimp, plants, microbes), nitrification O2 cost\n\n#### pH and Alkalinity\n- Simplified approximation for v1\n- Nitrification consumes alkalinity (0.1428 meq per mg N)\n- Photosynthesis lowers DIC during lit hours\n- Respiration/decomposition raise DIC\n- pH derived from alkalinity and DIC: `ph = clamp(6.3 + log10(max(alk_meq_l, 0.05)) - log10(max(dic_mmol_l, 0.02)), 5.5, 8.5)`\n\n#### Plant Growth (Guild-based)\n- FastStem: water-column nutrient user, faster growth\n- RootFeedingRosette: substrate-responsive, benefits from active substrate\n- Growth formula: `net_growth = biomass * max_rate * f_light * f_temp * min(f_n, f_p, f_c) * habitat_factor * (1 - crowding) - respiration - senescence`\n- Active substrate must boost rooted plants by 15%+ compared to inert sand\n\n#### Algae and Periphyton\n- Suspended algae: green water\n- Periphyton: attached biofilm complex on surfaces\n- Both compete with plants for light/nutrients\n- Periphyton provides shrimp food but becomes nuisance at high biomass\n\n#### Shrimp Population\n- Adults, juveniles, berried_females as aggregate counts\n- Condition (0..1) depends on: food, periphyton, DO, NH3, nitrite, temperature, GH, stability\n- Reproduction temperature anchor: best 22–26°C, clearly worse by 30°C, near-zero by 33°C\n- Molt stress rises from: low GH, abrupt chemistry changes, poor condition, thermal stress\n- Mortality probabilistic, increased by: NH3, nitrite, low DO, heat stress, molt stress, starvation\n\n#### Microfauna (Hidden State, Aggregated)\n- bacterivorous_protists, rotifers, nematodes, microcrustaceans\n- Effects: enhanced mineralization, periphyton grazing, reduced by shrimp predation\n- Not player-visible but mechanistically active\n\n---\n\n### 5. Simulation Time Model\n\n- **Base tick:** 1 hour per simulation tick\n- **Hourly update layer:** temperature, gas exchange, ammonia speciation, oxygen, decomposition, nitrification, feeding, light, hourly stress\n- **Daily update layer:** plant/algae biomass, microfauna turnover, shrimp condition/stress/reproduction, mortality checks, biofilter maturity\n- **Determinism:** explicit RNG (e.g., ChaCha8Rng) seeded from scenario, never thread-local RNG in core\n\n#### Hourly Update Pipeline (14 steps)\n1. Apply queued actions\n2. Update water volume from water changes\n3. Mix source water chemistry/temperature\n4. Update water temperature (ambient + heater)\n5. Compute light on/off\n6. Process feed and excretion\n7. Move detritus through decomposition/mineralization\n8. Update nitrification and nitrifier growth/decay\n9. Update DIC, alkalinity, pH\n10. Update dissolved oxygen\n11. Update hourly plant/periphyton photosynthesis/respiration\n12. Update shrimp hourly stress accumulators\n13. Emit hourly events\n14. Refresh observables\n\n#### Daily Update Pipeline (7 steps)\n1. Net plant biomass change\n2. Net algae/periphyton biomass change\n3. Microfauna turnover\n4. Shrimp condition, molt stress, reproduction, hatching, recruitment\n5. Mortality checks\n6. Biofilter maturity summary update\n7. Long-term stability metrics\n\n---\n\n### 6. Validation Rules\n\n- Percentages and fractions: 0.0..=1.0\n- Water change percent: 0.0..=100.0\n- Counts and grams: non-negative\n- No negative mass pools, populations\n- 0.0 ≤ health/maturity/stress ≤ 1.0\n- Temperature ≥ 0.0°C (unless scenario allows freezing)\n- Invalid actions return typed validation errors, no silent clamping\n\n---\n\n### 7. Data Files and Presets (to be created in tank_data)\n\n#### Source Water Profiles\n- soft_acidic\n- moderate\n- hard_shrimp\n- ro_like\n\nEach with: id, name, parameter values, optional [provenance] block (source_title, source_year, confidence, notes)\n\n#### Substrate Presets\n- inert_sand\n- inert_gravel\n- active_planted\n- coarse_porous\n\n#### Plant Guild Presets\n- fast_stem\n- root_rosette\n- moss_epiphyte (optional)\n- floating_plant (optional v1.1)\n\n#### Shrimp Pack\n- neocaridina_davidi (temperature optimum, high-temp penalty, biofilm grazing, GH dependence, juvenile sensitivity)\n\n#### Process Parameters\n- One default pack for all simulation parameters\n\n#### Scenarios\n- nano_cycle\n- medium_planted\n- warm_room\n\n#### Save File Format (JSON)\n- schema version\n- app version\n- full TankState\n- queued actions\n- RNG state\n\n---\n\n### 8. Acceptance Tests (Mandatory)\n\n1. **determinism_same_seed** - After 720 hours, identical seed/scenario/actions yield identical snapshots\n2. **save_load_resume** - Run 240h, save, load, run 480h more → matches uninterrupted 720h run\n3. **water_change_mass_balance** - 50% water change removes 50% of dissolved masses (±0.5%)\n4. **tank_size_response** - 10L tank shows 5x higher TAN spike than 100L tank after same feed; smaller tank temperature response faster\n5. **ambient_temperature_action** - Ambient temp rise causes gradual water temp rise, not instant; DO saturation decreases\n6. **cycling_seeded_vs_unseeded** - Seeded tanks reach stable faster than unseeded; unseeded shows TAN/nitrite peaks\n7. **overfeeding_effects** - Overfed tanks end with higher detritus, lower nightly DO, higher algae index\n8. **rooted_substrate_advantage** - RootFeedingRosette in active substrate has ≥15% higher biomass after 30 days than in inert sand\n9. **thermal_reproduction_penalty** - At 30°C vs 25°C, shrimp show ≥20% lower reproductive readiness and fewer juveniles over 60 days\n10. **event_generation** - Warm, overfed, weak-aeration scenario emits at least one of: AmmoniaWarning, OxygenDip, AlgaeRiskRising\n\n---\n\n### 9. TUI Screens (5 required)\n\n1. **Overview** - day/hour, temperature, pH, DO, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate, plant status, shrimp status, warnings\n2. **Chemistry** - detailed chemistry and recent trends\n3. **Biology** - plants, algae/periphyton, shrimp, biofilter maturity, hidden-state summaries\n4. **Actions** - forms for feed, water change, trim, siphon, clean filter, add/remove shrimp, change light, heater, ambient temp\n5. **Log** - chronological event list\n\n#### Time Controls\n- Advance 1 hour, 1 day, 1 week\n- Pause/autoadvance\n- Save/load\n- Quit\n\n---\n\n### 10. Implementation Milestones\n\n1. **Milestone 0** - Workspace skeleton, core types, config loading, RNG, save/load roundtrip\n2. **Milestone 1** - Geometry, temperature, heater, ambient temperature action\n3. **Milestone 2** - Dissolved pools, water changes, TDS/GH/KH/conductivity\n4. **Milestone 3** - Nitrogen cycle, oxygen dynamics, NH3 fraction, events\n5. **Milestone 4** - Substrate, plants, algae/periphyton, light, trim action\n6. **Milestone 5** - Shrimp population, reproduction, molt stress, microfauna\n7. **Milestone 6** - TUI MVP with all 5 screens\n8. **Milestone 7** - Regression scenarios, parameter audit, balancing\n\n---\n\n### 11. Scientific and Non-Negotiable Anchors\n\n**Must include:**\n1. Different tank sizes (impact on dilution, thermal inertia, stability)\n2. Ambient temperature as a real action (not cosmetic)\n3. Temperature-dependent water behavior\n4. pH/temperature-dependent ammonia risk\n5. Non-instant biological cycling (nitrification biomass-limited)\n6. Substrate effects (especially rooted plants)\n7. Plant vs algae competition\n8. Shrimp reproduction and failure states\n9. Deterministic save/load\n10. Text UI\n\n**Simplifications allowed in v1:**\n- Aggregated microfauna guilds instead of species-level\n- Approximate carbonate chemistry instead of full equilibrium\n- No explicit bacterial taxonomy beyond guilds\n- No spatial CFD or flow\n- One well-mixed water column\n- 1–3 substrate layers instead of continuous\n- Simple sex-ratio proxy for shrimp reproduction\n\n---\n\n### 12. Key Research Anchors\n\n1. Ammonia toxicity depends on pH, temperature, and unionized fraction\n2. Aquarium biofilters cycle at variable speeds (week 3–8 range observed)\n3. Comammox Nitrospira present in freshwater aquarium biofilters\n4. Rooted macrophytes draw from both sediment and water column\n5. Temperature and nutrient regime interact to affect plant/algae balance\n6. Protozoan grazing alters bacterial community and nutrient turnover\n7. Neocaridina davidi predates meiofauna, reshaping communities\n8. Neocaridina davidi reproduction inhibited at high sustained temperature (33°C suppresses spawning)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n**Current State:** Specification-complete, zero code. The workspace is ready for implementation to begin.\n\n**Key Deliverables Needed:**\n- Cargo workspace with 4 crates\n- Core deterministic simulation engine with full state model\n- Data-driven configuration loading (TOML presets)\n- Terminal UI (ratatui-based)\n- Complete regression test suite (10 mandatory tests)\n- All preset data files\n\n**Estimated Complexity:** Large, multi-month project with deep ecological and chemistry modeling, deterministic RNG, and TUI integration. The spec is comprehensive and actionable for incremental implementation across the 7-8 milestones defined."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acbccb342eb82c970 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 50101\ntool_uses: 21\nduration_ms: 95454</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aebe6b9c-6489-43f0-a717-82e4691947f3","uuid":"8811a4aa-ba05-40eb-a9f3-7a3216977afc","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Thoroughly explore the current state of this Rust workspace project at /root/tank-simulation. I need to understand:\n\n1. What Cargo workspace structure exists (Cargo.toml files, crate layout)\n2. What source files exist and their contents (especially src/lib.rs, src/main.rs files in each crate)\n3. What types, traits, and modules are already defined\n4. What tests exist\n5. What data/preset files exist (TOML files)\n6. What save/load functionality exists\n\nBe very thorough - check all crates mentioned: tank_core, tank_data, tank_tui, tank_scenarios. Check for any .rs files, .toml data files, test files, etc. Give me a complete picture of what code already exists.","agentId":"acbccb342eb82c970","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have a complete picture. Let me provide the comprehensive report:\n\n## Complete Workspace Exploration Report\n\n### Project Status\n\nThis is a **pre-implementation stage** of a Rust workspace project. No Cargo.toml files or source code (.rs files) exist yet. The project consists entirely of specification and planning documents.\n\n**Git Status:**\n- Current branch: `ralph/tank-sim`\n- Latest commits:\n  - `184e6c2` - chore(tank-sim): sync initial prompt inputs\n  - `5fc621c` - Initial commit with project spec\n\n**Tracked Files in Repository:**\n- `/root/tank-simulation/spec.md` (1,588 lines) - Comprehensive implementation specification\n- `/root/tank-simulation/.ralph/projects/tank-sim/project.toml` - Project metadata\n- `/root/tank-simulation/.ralph/projects/tank-sim/prompt.md` - Implementation prompt (v1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Cargo Workspace Structure (Planned but not yet created)\n\nThe spec defines a workspace to be created at `/root/tank-simulation/` with 4 crates under `crates/`:\n\n1. **tank_core** - Main simulation engine\n   - State types and models\n   - Update systems and equations\n   - Action application logic\n   - Save/load schema\n   - Deterministic RNG wrapper\n   - Unit tests\n   - No UI dependencies\n\n2. **tank_data** - Configuration and data loading\n   - TOML/JSON/RON preset assets\n   - Parameter loading and validation\n   - Preset packs for species and scenarios\n\n3. **tank_tui** - Terminal user interface\n   - Terminal dashboard (ratatui-based)\n   - Input mapping\n   - Time controls\n   - 5 main screens (Overview, Chemistry, Biology, Actions, Log)\n   - Charts/sparklines\n\n4. **tank_scenarios** - Test fixtures and scenarios\n   - Sample scenarios\n   - Regression validation scenarios\n   - Benchmark presets (nano, medium, warm-room)\n\n---\n\n### 2. Core Data Types (Defined in spec but not yet implemented)\n\n#### Main State Container\n```\nTankState\n├── meta: SimMeta\n├── geometry: TankGeometry\n├── environment: EnvironmentState\n├── hardware: HardwareState\n├── water: WaterState\n├── substrate: Vec<SubstrateLayerState>\n├── filter: FilterState\n├── plants: Vec<PlantGuildState>\n├── algae: AlgaeState\n├── microbes: MicrobeState\n├── microfauna: MicrofaunaState\n├── animals: AnimalState\n├── detritus: DetritusState\n├── schedules: ScheduleState\n├── observables: ObservableState\n├── events: Vec<SimEvent>\n└── rng: SimRng\n```\n\n#### Geometry (TankGeometry)\n- `length_cm, width_cm, height_cm, fill_height_cm`\n- `glass_thickness_mm, open_top: bool`\n- Derives: water_volume_l, surface_area_cm2, wall_area_cm2, footprint_area_cm2, surface/wall area ratios\n\n#### Water Chemistry (WaterState)\n- **Nitrogen pools:** ammonia_total_mg_n, nitrite_mg_n, nitrate_mg_n\n- **Phosphorus:** phosphate_mg_p\n- **Carbon/Oxygen:** dissolved_oxygen_mg, dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c\n- **Organic pools:** dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c, dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n\n- **Major ions:** calcium_mg, magnesium_mg, sodium_mg, potassium_mg, bicarbonate_mg, chloride_mg, sulfate_mg\n- **Derived:** alkalinity_meq, ph, conductivity_us_cm, tds_mg_l_display\n\n#### Hardware\n- **Light:** enabled, photoperiod_hours, intensity_index, schedule_start_hour\n- **Heater:** enabled, setpoint_c, max_watts, deadband_c, efficiency\n- **Filter/Pump:** flow_lph, media_surface_area_m2, cleanliness (0..1)\n- **Aeration:** enabled, intensity\n\n#### Substrate (LayerState - 1-3 layers)\n- kind: SubstrateKind (inert sand, inert gravel, active planted, coarse porous)\n- depth_cm, porosity, cec_index, organic_matter_g, trapped_detritus_g\n- nutrient stores (N, P), oxygen_penetration_index, colonizable_area_m2\n\n#### Filter State\n- maturity: f32 (0..1)\n- ammonia_oxidizer_biomass, nitrite_oxidizer_biomass, comammox_biomass\n- heterotroph_biomass, clogging\n\n#### Plants (Guild-based, not individual)\n- PlantGuildKind: FastStem, RootFeedingRosette, MossEpiphyte, FloatingPlant\n- For each guild: name, biomass_g_dry, health (0..1), nutrient_reserve_index (0..1)\n- shade_factor (0..1), root_fraction, growth_potential\n\n#### Algae State\n- suspended_algae_biomass (green water)\n- surface_film_biomass (glass algae)\n- periphyton_biomass (attached biofilm complex)\n- nuisance_index (0..1)\n\n#### Microbes (Hidden state)\n- decomposer_biomass\n- ammonia_oxidizer_biomass, nitrite_oxidizer_biomass, comammox_biomass\n- mineralization_capacity\n\n#### Microfauna (Aggregated)\n- bacterivorous_protists, rotifers, nematodes, microcrustaceans\n- visibility_index (0..1)\n\n#### Shrimp Population (AnimalState)\n- adults, juveniles, berried_females (counts as u32)\n- average_condition (0..1)\n- molt_stress_index (0..1)\n- reproductive_readiness (0..1)\n- egg_progress_days\n\n#### Detritus State\n- particulate_organic_matter_g\n- fine_detritus_g\n- bioavailable_food_g\n\n#### Events\n- day: u32, hour: u8, severity, kind, causes: Vec<String>, summary\n- Required event kinds: CycleProgressing, AmmoniaWarning, NitriteWarning, OxygenDip, AlgaeRiskRising, AlgaeBloom, BiofilmMaturityIncrease, ShrimpBerried, EggFailure, MoltStressWarning, FilterCleaningSetback, SubstrateFoulingWarning, StabilityImproving\n- Keep last 200 events in state, expose last 20 to UI\n\n---\n\n### 3. Public API Traits and Enums (Defined in spec)\n\n#### SimulationEngine Trait\n```rust\npub trait SimulationEngine {\n    fn apply_action(&mut self, action: PlayerAction) -> Result<(), SimError>;\n    fn step_hours(&mut self, hours: u32) -> Result<(), SimError>;\n    fn snapshot(&self) -> TankSnapshot;\n    fn full_state(&self) -> &TankState;\n}\n```\n\n#### PlayerAction Enum\n- `Feed { grams: f64 }`\n- `WaterChangePercent { percent: f64, source_profile_id: String }`\n- `TrimPlants { fraction: f64 }`\n- `SiphonDetritus { fraction: f64 }`\n- `CleanFilter { intensity: f64 }`\n- `AddShrimp { count: u32 }`\n- `RemoveShrimp { count: u32 }`\n- `ChangePhotoperiod { hours: f64 }`\n- `ChangeLightIntensity { intensity_index: f64 }`\n- `ChangeHeaterSetpoint { setpoint_c: f64 }`\n- `ChangeAmbientTemperature { target_c: f64 }` (MANDATORY)\n- `ChangeAeration { enabled: bool, intensity: f64 }`\n\n#### TankSnapshot (UI-Friendly View)\n- day: u32, temp_c, ph, do_mg_l, tan_mg_l, nh3_mg_l\n- nitrite_mg_l, nitrate_mg_l, phosphate_mg_l\n- gh_d, kh_d, conductivity_us_cm, tds_mg_l\n- plant_status: Vec<PlantStatusView>\n- shrimp_status: ShrimpStatusView\n- algae_risk: f32, biofilter_maturity: f32\n- recent_events: Vec<SimEvent> (last 20)\n\n#### SimSeed(u64) - Deterministic RNG seeding\n\n---\n\n### 4. Key Modeling Systems\n\n#### Temperature Model\n- Heat capacity proportional to water mass: `heat_capacity_j_per_k = volume_l * 4186.0`\n- Heat transfer: `ua_total_w_per_k = (k_surface * surface_area_m2 * top_factor) + (k_wall * wall_area_m2)`\n- Ambient heat: `q_ambient_w = ua_total_w_per_k * (ambient_temp_c - water_temp_c)`\n- Heater (when enabled and below setpoint): `q_heater_w = max_watts * efficiency`\n- Heater must never cool the tank\n- Delta: `delta_temp_c = (q_ambient_w + q_heater_w) * dt_s / heat_capacity_j_per_k`\n\n#### Nitrogen Cycle\n- Pathway: feed → detritus → mineralization → TAN → nitrite → nitrate\n- Nitrification must be biomass-limited, oxygen-limited, temperature/pH-sensitive\n- Monod-style rate: `rate = vmax * biomass * f_temp * f_pH * f_do * substrate / (k_substrate + substrate)`\n- Nitrifier guilds: ammonia oxidizers (AOA), nitrite oxidizers (NOB), comammox\n- O2 demand: 4.57 mg O2 per 1 mg N nitrified to nitrate\n- Alkalinity consumed: 0.1428 meq per 1 mg N nitrified\n\n#### Ammonia Speciation\n- pKa = 0.09018 + 2729.92 / (273.2 + temp_c)\n- fraction_nh3 = 1.0 / (1.0 + 10^(pKa - ph))\n- nh3_mg_l = tan_mg_l * fraction_nh3\n- NH3 drives toxicity more strongly than TAN\n\n#### Dissolved Oxygen\n- DO saturation table (linear interpolation):\n  - 0°C → 14.6 mg/L\n  - 10°C → 11.3 mg/L\n  - 20°C → 9.1 mg/L\n  - 30°C → 7.6 mg/L\n- Sources: photosynthesis (plants, periphyton), reaeration (kLa-based), aeration equipment\n- Sinks: respiration (shrimp, plants, microbes), nitrification O2 cost\n\n#### pH and Alkalinity\n- Simplified approximation for v1\n- Nitrification consumes alkalinity (0.1428 meq per mg N)\n- Photosynthesis lowers DIC during lit hours\n- Respiration/decomposition raise DIC\n- pH derived from alkalinity and DIC: `ph = clamp(6.3 + log10(max(alk_meq_l, 0.05)) - log10(max(dic_mmol_l, 0.02)), 5.5, 8.5)`\n\n#### Plant Growth (Guild-based)\n- FastStem: water-column nutrient user, faster growth\n- RootFeedingRosette: substrate-responsive, benefits from active substrate\n- Growth formula: `net_growth = biomass * max_rate * f_light * f_temp * min(f_n, f_p, f_c) * habitat_factor * (1 - crowding) - respiration - senescence`\n- Active substrate must boost rooted plants by 15%+ compared to inert sand\n\n#### Algae and Periphyton\n- Suspended algae: green water\n- Periphyton: attached biofilm complex on surfaces\n- Both compete with plants for light/nutrients\n- Periphyton provides shrimp food but becomes nuisance at high biomass\n\n#### Shrimp Population\n- Adults, juveniles, berried_females as aggregate counts\n- Condition (0..1) depends on: food, periphyton, DO, NH3, nitrite, temperature, GH, stability\n- Reproduction temperature anchor: best 22–26°C, clearly worse by 30°C, near-zero by 33°C\n- Molt stress rises from: low GH, abrupt chemistry changes, poor condition, thermal stress\n- Mortality probabilistic, increased by: NH3, nitrite, low DO, heat stress, molt stress, starvation\n\n#### Microfauna (Hidden State, Aggregated)\n- bacterivorous_protists, rotifers, nematodes, microcrustaceans\n- Effects: enhanced mineralization, periphyton grazing, reduced by shrimp predation\n- Not player-visible but mechanistically active\n\n---\n\n### 5. Simulation Time Model\n\n- **Base tick:** 1 hour per simulation tick\n- **Hourly update layer:** temperature, gas exchange, ammonia speciation, oxygen, decomposition, nitrification, feeding, light, hourly stress\n- **Daily update layer:** plant/algae biomass, microfauna turnover, shrimp condition/stress/reproduction, mortality checks, biofilter maturity\n- **Determinism:** explicit RNG (e.g., ChaCha8Rng) seeded from scenario, never thread-local RNG in core\n\n#### Hourly Update Pipeline (14 steps)\n1. Apply queued actions\n2. Update water volume from water changes\n3. Mix source water chemistry/temperature\n4. Update water temperature (ambient + heater)\n5. Compute light on/off\n6. Process feed and excretion\n7. Move detritus through decomposition/mineralization\n8. Update nitrification and nitrifier growth/decay\n9. Update DIC, alkalinity, pH\n10. Update dissolved oxygen\n11. Update hourly plant/periphyton photosynthesis/respiration\n12. Update shrimp hourly stress accumulators\n13. Emit hourly events\n14. Refresh observables\n\n#### Daily Update Pipeline (7 steps)\n1. Net plant biomass change\n2. Net algae/periphyton biomass change\n3. Microfauna turnover\n4. Shrimp condition, molt stress, reproduction, hatching, recruitment\n5. Mortality checks\n6. Biofilter maturity summary update\n7. Long-term stability metrics\n\n---\n\n### 6. Validation Rules\n\n- Percentages and fractions: 0.0..=1.0\n- Water change percent: 0.0..=100.0\n- Counts and grams: non-negative\n- No negative mass pools, populations\n- 0.0 ≤ health/maturity/stress ≤ 1.0\n- Temperature ≥ 0.0°C (unless scenario allows freezing)\n- Invalid actions return typed validation errors, no silent clamping\n\n---\n\n### 7. Data Files and Presets (to be created in tank_data)\n\n#### Source Water Profiles\n- soft_acidic\n- moderate\n- hard_shrimp\n- ro_like\n\nEach with: id, name, parameter values, optional [provenance] block (source_title, source_year, confidence, notes)\n\n#### Substrate Presets\n- inert_sand\n- inert_gravel\n- active_planted\n- coarse_porous\n\n#### Plant Guild Presets\n- fast_stem\n- root_rosette\n- moss_epiphyte (optional)\n- floating_plant (optional v1.1)\n\n#### Shrimp Pack\n- neocaridina_davidi (temperature optimum, high-temp penalty, biofilm grazing, GH dependence, juvenile sensitivity)\n\n#### Process Parameters\n- One default pack for all simulation parameters\n\n#### Scenarios\n- nano_cycle\n- medium_planted\n- warm_room\n\n#### Save File Format (JSON)\n- schema version\n- app version\n- full TankState\n- queued actions\n- RNG state\n\n---\n\n### 8. Acceptance Tests (Mandatory)\n\n1. **determinism_same_seed** - After 720 hours, identical seed/scenario/actions yield identical snapshots\n2. **save_load_resume** - Run 240h, save, load, run 480h more → matches uninterrupted 720h run\n3. **water_change_mass_balance** - 50% water change removes 50% of dissolved masses (±0.5%)\n4. **tank_size_response** - 10L tank shows 5x higher TAN spike than 100L tank after same feed; smaller tank temperature response faster\n5. **ambient_temperature_action** - Ambient temp rise causes gradual water temp rise, not instant; DO saturation decreases\n6. **cycling_seeded_vs_unseeded** - Seeded tanks reach stable faster than unseeded; unseeded shows TAN/nitrite peaks\n7. **overfeeding_effects** - Overfed tanks end with higher detritus, lower nightly DO, higher algae index\n8. **rooted_substrate_advantage** - RootFeedingRosette in active substrate has ≥15% higher biomass after 30 days than in inert sand\n9. **thermal_reproduction_penalty** - At 30°C vs 25°C, shrimp show ≥20% lower reproductive readiness and fewer juveniles over 60 days\n10. **event_generation** - Warm, overfed, weak-aeration scenario emits at least one of: AmmoniaWarning, OxygenDip, AlgaeRiskRising\n\n---\n\n### 9. TUI Screens (5 required)\n\n1. **Overview** - day/hour, temperature, pH, DO, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate, plant status, shrimp status, warnings\n2. **Chemistry** - detailed chemistry and recent trends\n3. **Biology** - plants, algae/periphyton, shrimp, biofilter maturity, hidden-state summaries\n4. **Actions** - forms for feed, water change, trim, siphon, clean filter, add/remove shrimp, change light, heater, ambient temp\n5. **Log** - chronological event list\n\n#### Time Controls\n- Advance 1 hour, 1 day, 1 week\n- Pause/autoadvance\n- Save/load\n- Quit\n\n---\n\n### 10. Implementation Milestones\n\n1. **Milestone 0** - Workspace skeleton, core types, config loading, RNG, save/load roundtrip\n2. **Milestone 1** - Geometry, temperature, heater, ambient temperature action\n3. **Milestone 2** - Dissolved pools, water changes, TDS/GH/KH/conductivity\n4. **Milestone 3** - Nitrogen cycle, oxygen dynamics, NH3 fraction, events\n5. **Milestone 4** - Substrate, plants, algae/periphyton, light, trim action\n6. **Milestone 5** - Shrimp population, reproduction, molt stress, microfauna\n7. **Milestone 6** - TUI MVP with all 5 screens\n8. **Milestone 7** - Regression scenarios, parameter audit, balancing\n\n---\n\n### 11. Scientific and Non-Negotiable Anchors\n\n**Must include:**\n1. Different tank sizes (impact on dilution, thermal inertia, stability)\n2. Ambient temperature as a real action (not cosmetic)\n3. Temperature-dependent water behavior\n4. pH/temperature-dependent ammonia risk\n5. Non-instant biological cycling (nitrification biomass-limited)\n6. Substrate effects (especially rooted plants)\n7. Plant vs algae competition\n8. Shrimp reproduction and failure states\n9. Deterministic save/load\n10. Text UI\n\n**Simplifications allowed in v1:**\n- Aggregated microfauna guilds instead of species-level\n- Approximate carbonate chemistry instead of full equilibrium\n- No explicit bacterial taxonomy beyond guilds\n- No spatial CFD or flow\n- One well-mixed water column\n- 1–3 substrate layers instead of continuous\n- Simple sex-ratio proxy for shrimp reproduction\n\n---\n\n### 12. Key Research Anchors\n\n1. Ammonia toxicity depends on pH, temperature, and unionized fraction\n2. Aquarium biofilters cycle at variable speeds (week 3–8 range observed)\n3. Comammox Nitrospira present in freshwater aquarium biofilters\n4. Rooted macrophytes draw from both sediment and water column\n5. Temperature and nutrient regime interact to affect plant/algae balance\n6. Protozoan grazing alters bacterial community and nutrient turnover\n7. Neocaridina davidi predates meiofauna, reshaping communities\n8. Neocaridina davidi reproduction inhibited at high sustained temperature (33°C suppresses spawning)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n**Current State:** Specification-complete, zero code. The workspace is ready for implementation to begin.\n\n**Key Deliverables Needed:**\n- Cargo workspace with 4 crates\n- Core deterministic simulation engine with full state model\n- Data-driven configuration loading (TOML presets)\n- Terminal UI (ratatui-based)\n- Complete regression test suite (10 mandatory tests)\n- All preset data files\n\n**Estimated Complexity:** Large, multi-month project with deep ecological and chemistry modeling, deterministic RNG, and TUI integration. The spec is comprehensive and actionable for incremental implementation across the 7-8 milestones defined."}],"totalDurationMs":95454,"totalTokens":50101,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":44342,"output_tokens":5354,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":405},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
